<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles the Fat</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">839–888</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles the Fat was a Carolingian ruler who briefly reunited the realms of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire</a> between 881 and 888 CE. His reign was undermined when he paid tribute to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Vikings</a> besieging <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> rather than fight them. He was deposed shortly before his death, and the empire fragmented permanently.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-the-fat.jpg" alt="Charles the Fat" width="302" height="291" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sceau_de_Charles_le_gros.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
